{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update41.json\", \"summary\": \"With the run's window down to its last minute, I recorded the second durable finding as knowledge rather than starting work that could not be verified: a follower forwards MsgReadIndex to the leader it knows (no term is attached, since the library treats that message as local), and if that leader is a removed leader of a single-voter configuration it answers through the singleton shortcut with a MsgReadIndexResp carrying its own frozen commit index - so the stale index does not stay inside the removed leader but crosses the wire and is consumed as the forwarding node's own read state, after which that node serves reads that can miss entries the actual leader had already committed. The entry cites the source ranges for the shortcut, the forwarding branch and the response constructor, and events 1-7 of check 815614d0. Validation reports valid with a knowledge entry created. Both this entry and the previous one (the corrected bound that the end of the exposure follows from a replacement leader existing, not from the quorum option) now sit alongside the Q2 and Q1 accounts, so the two findings that outlive the prose are reviewable rather than buried in interpretation text.\"}"}}
